# answer-stats verification — raw literal log

Scope: privacy-safe answer-aggregate endpoint + player percentages + comment
toggle. No prose verdicts below — command + literal output only.

Code footprint:
  src/routes/questions.routes.ts         (+GET /questions/:id/answer-stats)
  src/routes/sessions.routes.ts         (+correctOptionIds, practice-only)
  web/src/lib/types.ts                  (+correctOptionIds, +AnswerStatsResponse)
  web/src/components/AnswerOption.tsx   (+isCorrectOption/pickPercentage/revealCorrectness)
  web/src/components/QuestionCard.tsx   (+stats caption, comment toggle)
  web/src/app/sessions/[id]/page.tsx    (+stats fetch best-effort, key reset)

Privacy design (stated, then proven): response carries ONLY
{questionId, attempts, options:[{optionId, percentage}]} — no user/session ids,
no timestamps, no per-attempt rows. Small-sample rule: 0 attempts →
options:[] (UI hides block); >=1 → percentages + labeled attempt count.

Screenshots (live localhost:3001 DOM):
  docs/verification/answer-stats-percentages.png   (0/0/0/100 + caption + toggle)
  docs/verification/answer-stats-comment.png       (open panel, existing text)
  docs/verification/answer-stats-exam.png          (Répondu, no %%, no toggle)
  docs/verification/answer-stats-noexplanation.png (feedback, no toggle)

